			<div class="content" id="post-content-4802510">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> You know it!</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong> A keter-class SCP is the initial article, but through correspondence and addenda the anomaly is rendered neutralized. Throughout the article, there are autopsies, emails, RAISA reports and otherwise to give a more clear depiction of the interpretation of the Foundation used here.</p>
<p><strong>Layout:</strong> Initial article, various reports, autopsies, etc. Then a final log on the current condition of the SCP after a breach at a foundation site.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A file is spreading throughout the internet. Downloading it infects the host, and whenever they inseminate/are inseminated, that child rapidly and horrifically mutates into an incredibly hostile organism, with computer parts and grossly elongated limbs stretching out from its body. This causes a sort of epidemic, one that the Foundation is just barely able to contain. A series of logs and records of outbreaks, autopsies, interviews, and correspondence slowly reveal how extreme this &quot;pandemic&quot; is- the Foundation traces it to a cult leader, who is trying to use the file as a means of birthing a new god. Notably, we can see as the logs progress how the Foundation is using emergency measures to increase it's power- organizations like the UIU and even the GOC are starting to defer to the Foundation in these circumstances, because it would seem that only the Foundation has the technology to contain it. Near the end, the cult leader &quot;creator&quot; of the file implies that he wasnt the one who made it, but he was given it by the Foundation. Essentially, I want a sort of slow reveal that this was a power grab by the Foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
I'm definitely going for body horror here, and I think I may drop the autopsy for the sake of more action-oriented logs. I'm trying a lot of new things with formatting in the article itself, so if you'd like to check it out, let me know.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

