<p>Ah, looking for a critique, are you?</p>
<p>Well&#8230;how about I&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+Give&nbsp;you&nbsp;one?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-yeet</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>To summarize how I feel about this idea: I dig it to all hell and back, but I wanna go a little more in depth on that.</p>
<p>Everything pre-Foundation infection makes sense and is well-explained.</p>
<p>Weird cyborg amalgamate babies are found hither and thither, weird infectious website is the reason why, and now these messed up cyber babies are popping up everywhere. Foundation shuts it all down. I see no major issues with that bit.</p>
<p>But the part where the Foundation itself kinda just&#8230;oofs this thing into their own personnel by accident? I don't <em>quite</em> follow.</p>
<p>The download file is what infects people, right? Does it need to be opened and interacted with, or does it give a computer a radius of infection once it's on a system?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Site Director leaves the -3 instances alive, including his wife and child. But it's time to move on. They are incinerated. This leads back to the anomalous item first seen on opening the article- 124 jars of strange, anomalous ash that moves in odd patterns, one of which is stored in the office of Site-981's Site Director.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ouch. This could make for a great emotional scene to tie this all back up. But again, I can't imagine an organization as competent as the Foundation just oof-ing this thing into their personnel because oops!</p>
<p>I like everything else about this concept except for that Foundation incompetency.</p>
<p>One last thing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No, it's not complete. I'm assuming it can only be greenlighted if it's 'done', then I put it on the draft critique forum- that part didn't seem clear.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Create concept, post concept, get crit, fix idea up over time until two reviewers with Greenlight privileges deem it worthy of a Greenlight. Once two Greenlights are achieved, you unlock the draft forums so you can start getting in-depth critique there. By default, putting 'Yes' next to <strong>Seeking Greenlights</strong> is what a new author is supposed to do if they want Greenlights. Which I assume you do :P</p>
<p>That said, I hope I helped and I bid you a lovely day, partner!</p>
<p>👍👍👍</p>
</div>
