<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First up: you only have an elevator pitch here; you're currently missing the 'Central Narrative', 'Hook/Attention-grabber' and 'Additional Notes' sections of the format.</p>
<p>Beyond this, my core concern is that a lot of the narrative you've laid out is very passive: it feels like a sequence of events that happen rather than a story because there's no-one like, actively moving the story from one event to the next so much as just, a series of actions causing it, if that makes sense? It doesn't help that it feels like this idea is hella overcomplex: there's a lot of moving parts and iterations and it makes following what's going on very challenging.</p>
<p>The large number of iterations doesn't necessarily feel like a great idea here: it adds a lot of complexity without really feeling like they're doing much that just, adding some updates to the end of the file wouldn't achieve better, y'know?</p>
<p>I don't dislike any part of the anomaly in particular, but it also doesn't feel like any part is by itself that interesting: it feels like a bunch of ideas that have been already done cobbled together; and I'm left wondering if there'd be a good way to streamline this down a lot and add the focus it's missing; but I don't really have any suggestions for how to do that tbh.</p>
</div>
