			<div class="content" id="post-content-4819599">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Behold!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is an anomalous file capable of generating websites (SCP-XXXX-1) advertised as support blogs for those suffering from infertility. These websites carry copies of the file, where it is advertised as a &quot;cure&quot; to infertility. These files, when downloaded, infect the &quot;owner&quot; of the host computer, making them an instance of SCP-XXXX-2.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This part feels somewhat disconnected from the rest of the anomaly, in a way. I feel like either you lean all in on the pseudo-science behind these fake cures, like magazines, youtube videos, Facebook ads, so on. Make SCP-XXXX more akin to an infection.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It infected everyone stationed at the site, identifying them all as the &quot;owner&quot;. The SCP-XXXX-3 instances develop as normal, so nothing was noticed, beyond a sudden increase in pregnancies, as SCP-XXXX-2 instances have a memetic compulsion to reproduce.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>At this point, I feel like this gets bloated. I'd either focus on the anomaly affecting the general populous, or the story of the Foundation. As a reader, you're going to have a climax with the MTF log, then you basically restart the pacing. This could be jarring.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Head Researcher- it's implying the ashes are of the SCP-XXXX-3 instance his wife bore.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I like this, oddly. Again though, you're telling another story, this one being focused on a single character or person. What story is the most important for you to tell?</p>
<hr />
<p>Overall, this needs to be toned down to one single arc. Both for your sake as a writer and for the sake of your audience. Focus on the story you want to tell, how will you explore that?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

